abstract={Relevance. In September 2023, airborne laser scanning and aerial photography were carried out using an unmanned aerial vehicle on the territory of the Makazhoy basin, where the carbon landfill of the Kadyrov Chechen State University is located. As a result, a high-precision digital elevation model (DEM) was compiled for sites with an area of about 170 hectares located on opposite macro slopes of the basin at comparable absolute heights (1700-2200 m). Subsequent processing of the DEM using the ArcGIS software made it possible to quantify the microrelief of the test sites, as well as to identify terraces within the natural mountain slopes. The aim is a comparative analysis of the relief of the northern and southern macroscopes of the Makazhoy basin to assess the influence of morphometric characteristics of the territory (height, steepness, exposure) on the terracing of the slopes. Materials and methods. The work is based on aerial laser scanning and aerial photography performed by UAVs in the fall of 2023. Their subsequent processing made it possible to create a highly detailed digital model, which was analyzed in a GIS environment. The terraces were mapped using a combined method combining manual and semi-automatic vectorization. Results. The comparative analysis revealed quantitative differences in the relief of the macroslopes and, accordingly, their development potential. Terraces occupy 46 % of the northern macroslope, which is gentler and more humid, while on the steep and dry southern macroslope they cover only 26 %. Conclusions. The obtained results create a scientific basis for developing practical measures for rational nature management, including the regulation of pasture loads and the implementation of regenerative livestock farming principles within the carbon polygon. © 2025, Geophysical Institute of the Vladikavkaz Scientific Centre of the Russian Academy of Sciences. All rights reserved.},
